A||||3||GT Bastard||Lower voltage after new Alternator...||||8||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||04-24-2000||06:39 PM||||After replacing my alternator, my volt meter stays at about 12-13 volts... Is this normal. My old alternator kept me at almost the max redline!(which is one of the reasons I thought there was a problem with it.) It's a brand new battery.  The alternator is a Delco 94 amp.  The car doesn't seem to lose any power after driving for an hour or so, but it just seems to hang kinda low, and the other alternator was EXACTLY the same brand and model.  thanks guys...||||reg||8
Z||000001||DiggityDan||04-24-2000||07:03 PM||||There was something definately wrong with your old alternator, or more specific, the regulator. The regulator holds voltage at about 12.5 - 13, when working properly. You're probably lucky you didn't fry something. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-24-2000||07:09 PM||||check it at the battery. A battery under charre should show 13-14 volts. don't cound on the dash gauge being exact.<P>you can also stop at many parts stores wich will test for free just to verify it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||04-24-2000||07:10 PM||||Cool, thanks Dan.  I think someone mentioned the regulator could do that before, and that was why I replaced it(also because it just died completely!)  I suspected that overcharging killed my battery because the battery worked great in another car and died shortly after transplanting it in my GT.  Maybe that wasn't the cause of the battery, I don't know...  <P>||||reg||1
